{
  "decision": "NO_CHANGE",
  "workflow_yaml": null,
  "rationale": "The workflow already implements the evidence-supported optimizations that fit it. P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT (bound jobs with a custom timeout, measured 26.8% elapsed savings in the cited experiment) is already present on every job: resolve_xrpld_image (2 min), build-and-lint (10 min), unit (10 min), integration (10 min), and browser (10 min). P-LIT-GHA-CACHE (cache dependency downloads) is already applied via actions/cache@v4 keyed on package-lock.json and node version in build-and-lint, unit, integration, and browser jobs. The resolve_xrpld_image job does not install npm dependencies, so dependency caching is not relevant there. Other patterns are either ci_service-scope (not workflow-yaml changes), estimated/synthetic rather than measured for this context, or have contraindications (e.g., every matrix outcome is required, valid slow runs could exceed a tighter limit, and CI history is not a measured baseline). No additional supported, safe, minimal change is warranted while preserving build and test coverage.",
  "evidence_ids": ["P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT", "P-LIT-GHA-CACHE"]
}
